Subject: [PATCH 5/5] src/lab-process-mail: Take the base from LAB_BASE_BRANCH
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: mxzutorvxrszomtttzlrrvpplpyuutvk

lab-process-mail always based work on trunk. That suits an ordinary
contributor, but an operator's own assistant does better seeing the
tree the operator sees, and Pat stages every candidate for trunk on
b/dev. Work based only on trunk misses those commits, so patches that
build on them must be assembled by hand or rebased later.

LAB_BASE_BRANCH names the revset to base work on, and defaults to
trunk(), so an unconfigured run behaves as it did. The agent is told
the base it was given, since the prompt's rebase and new-change steps
depend on it. When b/dev is rebuilt upstream, work on it follows the
new head and the old b/dev commits are dropped rather than copied.
